/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/Bisulfite-formation.dat -- the first dissociation of sulfurous acid, written from the master:
      H2SO3  <=>  Bisulfite + H+
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 1.857, dH1 = -17.80 kJ/mol, dCp -272 J/mol/K (grade BBA)
      pK2 = 7.172, dH2 = -3.65 kJ/mol, dCp -262 J/mol/K (grade BAB)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  This record carries the first step (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
  Goldberg writes the neutral acid H2SO3; the species H2SO3 is the formal stoichiometric acid (aqueous SO2).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species Bisulfite; masters ( { ion H2SO3; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } );
      logK25 -1.857; dH -17800; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.59, p. 344: pK1 1.857, dH1 -17.80 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
